#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""aos-frontend - one local page that shows every agent and proc on the daemon table as a tree,
the user-zone letters waiting for the user (answer them right there), and lets the user say
one line to an agent. Phase 0 + phase 1 of proto8/thinking/2026-11/14/view-1114 (no model anywhere):
phase 1 adds team folders, the relay mailbox (letters with body.zone "view/1") and an aide that only carries facts.

usage: aos-frontend [--port 8767] [--home DIR] serve     run the page on 127.0.0.1 (foreground)
       aos-frontend [--home DIR] snapshot                 print the tree as JSON once and exit
       aos-frontend [--home DIR] init                     make the home folder (keeps what exists)
       aos-frontend [--home DIR] ingest                   one pass over the relay mailbox (serve does this every poll)
  captains (claude agents with Bash):
       aos-frontend note [--team T] [--on NAME] STATUS TEXT   STATUS: start progress done blocked decision handoff ask
       aos-frontend decide [--team T] FILE                a user-zone letter body -> teams/T/outbox/<id>.json; prints the id
       aos-frontend match REPLY_FOLDER                    is the zone's answered letter the one the captain wrote?
       aos-frontend aide-def [--template DIR] PATH        make the team's aide definition PATH: copy the agent-fsm template
                                                      (--template, else $AOS_HOME/templates/agent-fsm), then lay every
                                                      file of aide-def/ over it (not _index.json); a relative PATH starts
                                                      at $AOS_WS when set, else here
  the aide (an on_clock hook of agent <team>-aide-1; event JSON on stdin):
       aos-frontend aide-tick [--team T]                  pass outbox files, a report when facts changed, a beat each 15 min
  team default: --team, else the basename of $AOS_STACK if it is a name on the daemon table
  (aide-tick: the aide's name without -aide-N)

home: --home > $AOS_VIEW_HOME > ~/.aos/view
  config.json   optional: {"parents": {"name": "parent"}, "parent_rules": [["ok-*", "repo-aos"]],
                           "say_log": "path", "poll_s": 20}
  mailbox/      the relay mailbox (aos-post layout); teams send replies here, the page only reads it
  state/        activity.json (when each agent last changed), say.jsonl (default say log),
                teams/<team>.json (latest report, last beat, latest post), passed/<team>/<id>.json (receipts)
  teams/<team>/ aide.json {team, parent, leader, aide, tags}, notes.jsonl, outbox/<id>.json, outbox/sent/,
                sent.jsonl {id, at, sha256}, send_failed, seq, aide_state.json
  done/<YYYY-MM>/, rejected/  processed / refused view/1 letters (moved out of mailbox/, never deleted)
  token         CSRF token (0600), made on first serve
Only reads official interfaces: aos-agent ctl ls / ctl state / history ls, the user zone
(through aos-user's own zone.py, read-only) and its own relay mailbox. Writes only by running
aos-user answer/reply/ok and aos-agent say. Stdlib only.
GET /api/slash_results?name=NAME returns recent page slash commands and their reply states.
"""
